# Clean Code and Architecture Principles

## 1. File Size and Modularity

- NO component file should exceed 150-200 lines of code.
- If a component grows too large, extract the logic into Custom Hooks (e.g., `useMyFeature.ts`) and the UI into sub-components.
- Single Responsibility Principle (SRP): One component = one visual or logical task.

## 2. Structure and Reusability (Local Design System)

- Never hardcode a UI component that could be reused (cards, section headers, layout wrappers).
- Strictly separate "Dumb/UI" components (which only display props, without complex state logic) from "Smart/Containers" components (which fetch data or manage state).
- Shared components must go into `src/components/ui` or `src/components/shared`.
- Page-specific components must remain close to that page (e.g., `src/app/dashboard/_components/`).

## 3. Strict Typing (TypeScript)

- Explicitly export and type all component `Props`.
- Do NOT use the `any` type. Use generics if necessary.
